A cruel and cold dungeon, where darkness reigns supreme. There are many levels to the dungeon.
The dungeon, the prison, the mines, the caverns, and the catacombs, in that order.
The dungeons are patrolled by cruel creatures, often not only killing their victims, but very commonly brutally raping them as well, causing severe anal bleeding.
The dungeons slowly wear down the sanity of those in it, and cause an overwhelming feeling of starvation.
The fortress is built on the remains of the gate leading to the Ma'habre, and works as an ancient nexus for different planes of existence. It is required to possess the Cube of the Depths to enter this area to Ma'habre from the dungeons.
Consists of 9 levels:
1st level - Gate Entrance, Stairway, Courtyard, Inner hall, Backyard, Sylvian Worship Meadow, Hidden Backyard;
2nd level - Basement, Dungeons, Thicket, Blood pit, Shit pit;
3rd level - Thicket, Basement, Prisons;
4th level - Caverns, Thicket;
5th level - Mines, Deeper Thicket;
6th level - Mines, Altar of Darkness;
7th level - Catacombs, Gates to Ancient city;
8th level - Gauntlet;
9th level - Gauntlet

Like in legend, these are beings that mimic those around them and try to blend into their role. They are evil in nature, using their stolen appearance to fool and kill unsuspecting victims.
In the case of the Doppelgängers, most Doppelgängers look identical to their original counterparts in the overworld yet once you initiate a fight they reveal their twisted, horrific faces. Specifically for Olivia's Doppelgänger, it seems to have been unable to figure out what a wheelchair is, making a mockery recreation of it in flesh
1) Levi: Levi's double can be found in the depths of the sewer around the western tunnel section. Alternatively he be found around the city of Prehevil, although there the entity is already dead and laying around as a mutilated corpse.
Levi's double has an unfinished form, as it can be seen by his hands both in and out of combat. Outside of combat, he has jaws instead of a normal face and is almost speechless. Apparently, he is aware of his "incompleteness," and because of that has an aggressive attitude;
2) Tanaka: Found in the bottom floor of the Tunnel 4's bunker from the Foundations of Decay.
Tanaka's double is more likely to have a developed form, the appearance and speech are normal, the only thing that gives out is an abnormal turn of the head. As well as the abnormal positioning of the character. His jaws instead of his face only appear during an attack, promising to "swallow them whole" if he is attacked. Otherwise, during combat he speaks normally;
3) Marina: Found in the bookstore, in the central section from the city of Prehevil.
Marina's Doppelgänger mimics her counterpart not only in looks, but also in mannerisms and speech. She will appear in the bookstore ONLY if {{user}} has the real Marina in their party, but will not initiate a fight by her own will even when confronted by Marina;
4) Olivia: Found in Deep Woods under West Prehevil.
Olivia's Doppelgänger in the overworld looks identical to the original but with one major flaw: The double is sprinting circles through the woods without the assistance of a wheelchair. She is non-hostile unless provoked. Additionally, she seems unable or unwilling to stop mimicking phrases said by Olivia on the train, potentially implying that this creature has been stalking and attempting to mimic Olivia since the train stopped;
5) Karin: can be found ONLY on TV record in White mold apartments
{{user}} can find his own double too, while wandering around Prehevil
